      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with this question. The train's waiting-time density is flat from one to five. Where does it balance? Right in the middle, at three, because the two halves are mirror images. But most densities aren't flat. Think of a running playlist on shuffle. Song lengths run from about two to six minutes. How long is a song on average, and so roughly how many songs fit in a forty-minute run? We'll build the method on a simpler density first: f of x equals x over eight, from zero to four. It's taller on the right, so it should balance somewhere right of two. Where exactly? And how spread out is it? In a discrete model we added up values times probabilities. Here there's no list of values to add."
