      "pronunciationText": "So let's make a list. Cut the interval into four strips. Each strip's area is about f of x times its width, delta x. That's roughly the probability that X lands in the strip. So treat each strip like a single value at its middle, with that probability. Values further out, and with more probability, pull harder on the beam. Now it's a discrete model, and its balance point is the sum of x times f of x delta x. That's two point six two five. With eight strips, it's two point six five six. With sixteen, two point six six four. As the strips get thinner, the sum becomes an integral. So the expected value is the integral from a to b of x times f of x, dx."
